{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104715-gritty-dirty-dangerous-magic","id":1104715,"title":"Gritty, Dirty, Dangerous Magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-17T06:53:27-07:00","id":1104715,"title":"Gritty, Dirty, Dangerous Magic","content":"I love this quote from this <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd/page3\">thread</a> , and would love to run a Mage Chronicle at a bit lower power level, more gritty and dangerous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In order for mage to have &quot;Consequences of Power&quot; and &quot;Temptation of Power&quot; as tropes, you actually need to be short on power so you are tempted to...Reach. Which is why I think that my preferred model of play will be low (3 and less) Arcanas while utilizing tons of Reach options. Which is great, because in case of some Arcanas (looking at you, Death and Spirit) you needed like 3 to get anything useful, and then at 4 you suddenly became super powerful, outstripping other Arcanas in power due to flexibility of these high powered options. </div> </div> </div>What would you need to tinker with to make your chronicle work this way?<br /> <br /> I feel that Hurt Locker would have lots of good stuff for making violence a bit more gritty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T06:59:15-07:00","id":1104716,"title":"","content":"I found &quot;Faustian Magic&quot; and &quot;Mad with Power.&quot; Both seem like pretty cool hacks but they're for 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T07:28:44-07:00","id":1104721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104715-gritty-dirty-dangerous-magic?p=1104716#post1104716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found &quot;Faustian Magic&quot; and &quot;Mad with Power.&quot; Both seem like pretty cool hacks but they're for 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Where can they be found?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T07:37:20-07:00","id":1104725,"title":"","content":"Oh, they're in the Mage Chronicler's Guide (1e).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T09:38:14-07:00","id":1104751,"title":"","content":"If running in this kind of setting, I would:<br /> 1) Cap Arcana at 3 Dots<br /> 2) Allow casting above Arcana rating at a cost of 1 Reach per dot you are below the Practice<br /> 2a) You would have no Free Reach when doing this<br /> 2b) How far you could reach for this would be limited by Gnosis - no Reaching to a 5-dot Practice unless you have 5 Gnosis<br /> <br /> IE a Disciple can cast a Making spell if they have 5 Gnosis, but they're going to have no free reach and will be throwing at minimum 6 dice of Paradox, more if it's instant cast, sensory, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T11:57:56-07:00","id":1104807,"title":"","content":"You could also allow Paradox to accumulate. Every spell after the first in a scene adds 1 persistent Paradox, which drops at the rate of 1 per Scene (or day, if you are mean). Or let the ST bank them, then hit characters when it would hurt. Some characters might even grow bold when no consequence seems forthcoming.<br /> <br /> Another thought. To some degree this might already be in effect, but when Paradox is released, you could have it affect targets according to the source's Nimbus/Sympathetic links. Characters might release their Paradoxes repeatedly to no visible consequence... until they visit their cousin. Or at least what once was their cousin before the Abyss took hold of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-17-2017, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T16:31:42-07:00","id":1105217,"title":"","content":"Another idea might be to run primarily/only Proximi, augmenting them with little increases and hacks here or there (check out the Homebrew Mage Merit thread for some merit based ideas).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T06:42:32-07:00","id":1105366,"title":"","content":"donno, never had problem being powerful at 3 dots. particularly with death and spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T09:30:54-07:00","id":1105424,"title":"","content":"Really, grit and danger have very little to do with mechanics, and more to do with mood and theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T09:40:53-07:00","id":1105428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104715-gritty-dirty-dangerous-magic?p=1105424#post1105424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, grit and danger have very little to do with mechanics, and more to do with mood and theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanics can make that easier or harder, though. Being able to destroy opposition with little effort or risk decreases (or at least desensitizes) the feeling of danger. Yeah, you can up the opposition, but that starts the strain a ST's options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T09:53:11-07:00","id":1105433,"title":"","content":"The mechanics in Mage aren't working to make grit and danger harder to pull off, in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T11:52:07-07:00","id":1105475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104715-gritty-dirty-dangerous-magic?p=1105424#post1105424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, grit and danger have very little to do with mechanics, and more to do with mood and theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don\u00b4t forget also many supernaturals have their powers because they need them for what they are up against:<br /> <br /> Werewolves have to fight against powerful entities like spirits, hosts or Idigam, who want to turn the Earth into their playground.<br /> Changelings live in fear from the implacable Hunstmen who will never stop until the runaway slaves are brought back to Faerie.<br /> The God Machine is out there to get you. For Demons this is not paranoia, but a fact.<br /> <br /> Mages ???","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T12:20:55-07:00","id":1105483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104715-gritty-dirty-dangerous-magic?p=1105475#post1105475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages ???</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure what your comment has to do with mine, but to answer this specific question, Mages have to deal with reality and the many facets of it that hates them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T13:01:47-07:00","id":1105492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104715-gritty-dirty-dangerous-magic?p=1105483#post1105483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not sure what your comment has to do with mine, but to answer this specific question, Mages have to deal with reality and the many facets of it that hates them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except Mages can often tell said reality to shut up and go sit in the corner. Paradox is the only bite-back, and Paradox can be mitigated fairly easily.<br /> <br /> Mages often have to opt into their deterrent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T13:06:24-07:00","id":1105494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104715-gritty-dirty-dangerous-magic?p=1105492#post1105492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except Mages can often tell said reality to shut up and go sit in the corner. Paradox is the only bite-back, and Paradox can be mitigated fairly easily.<br /> <br /> Mages often have to opt into their deterrent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe I said facets, plural, Paradox is just one facet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T13:47:06-07:00","id":1105506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104715-gritty-dirty-dangerous-magic?p=1105494#post1105494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe I said facets, plural, Paradox is just one facet.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the others? Seers are just rival Mages, not aspects of reality, and not universally applicable. The God-Machine, maybe, but that's outside of strictly Mage scope. The Abyss is anti-reality, and generally encountered as a function of Paradox. Do you mean the mechanics of the game itself?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T13:50:01-07:00","id":1105508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104715-gritty-dirty-dangerous-magic?p=1105492#post1105492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except Mages can often tell said reality to shut up and go sit in the corner.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Mages in the abstract&quot; is not the same thing as &quot;mages as a collective whole.&quot; The Awakened do not have a singular Arcanum rating that lets them do everything with equal skill and delicacy, and haste or indecision being responsible for the bulk of the direct problems with their powers does not translate to &quot;mages don't have to worry about reality&quot; outside the absurdly unlikely scenario where a given character does everything perfectly.<br /> <br /> Mages handle power that attracts complications in a world with a great many moving parts. They're jugglers that put out a joking call for chainsaws in a venue where the chainsaw emporium is eager to advertise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T14:03:52-07:00","id":1105509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104715-gritty-dirty-dangerous-magic?p=1105506#post1105506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seers are just rival Mages, not aspects of reality, and not universally applicable.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about the people they work for?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T15:23:01-07:00","id":1105532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104715-gritty-dirty-dangerous-magic?p=1105506#post1105506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the others? Seers are just rival Mages, not aspects of reality, and not universally applicable. The God-Machine, maybe, but that's outside of strictly Mage scope. The Abyss is anti-reality, and generally encountered as a function of Paradox. Do you mean the mechanics of the game itself?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that the setting is filled with a lot of things that are dangerous to Mages regardless of the level of power that they accrue. A change in mechanics isn't necessary to make that obvious to the characters or the players. Especially, since &quot;gritty&quot; and &quot;dangerous&quot; are feelings. Mechanics don't evoke feelings, thats in the realm of a good ST using the setting and narrative skills to evoke a theme and mood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T17:55:25-07:00","id":1105562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104715-gritty-dirty-dangerous-magic?p=1105532#post1105532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean that the setting is filled with a lot of things that are dangerous to Mages regardless of the level of power that they accrue. A change in mechanics isn't necessary to make that obvious to the characters or the players. Especially, since &quot;gritty&quot; and &quot;dangerous&quot; are feelings. Mechanics don't evoke feelings, thats in the realm of a good ST using the setting and narrative skills to evoke a theme and mood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. But it can easily get undermined when &quot;You are cornered by 4 thugs with knives out for your blood.&quot; turns into &quot;I render them all comatose with 1 action/spell. What now?&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes, you can up the ante, but every added layer of potency adds more risk - Mages for all their power are also more fragile than many other supernaturals. Too far and it turns into Rocket Tag. Building survivable opponents that can't be undone in a spell or two by a single Mage (let alone a Cabal) take more time and effort. Nothing insurmountable, but something the ready access to power <i>does</i> render harder than the alternative.<br /> <br /> You can still throw consequences at them that they can't easily fix, of course. Raising the dead isn't easy, so dead contact/allies works, but that runs the risk of alienating the characters (and possibly the Players) from making connections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T18:44:36-07:00","id":1105568,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> Yes, using dumb opponents or being a dumb ST will tend to make the players look a lot more powerful than they actually are which can damage your ability to evoke the feelings of grit and danger. That still isn't a flaw in the mechanics though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 06-19-2017, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T21:44:23-07:00","id":1105592,"title":"","content":"To your thugs example, consider prepending one of the following:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The mage needs to remain in cover as a Sleepwalker to achieve a mission objective.<br /> There is a witchhunter in the area.<br /> The street-facing camera in the shop across the street catches the mage's eye.<br /> A cop (or just some random helpful soul) runs up to help the hapless stranger. <br /> There are some vampires in the area that are hunting mages. </div> <br /> Context and theme interact quite a lot. I agree with Mrmdubois that there isn't any major need for changing the rules to achieve your stated objective.<br /> <br /> (Also: Mages are <i>not</i> aspects of the setting's reality? Ha!)<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, if you seek to make things more risky, some ideas:<ul><li>Increase Paradox. This can be accomplished in a few ways. Reducing safe Reach, for example, or making spells always roll Paradox. Increasing the rate of growth from Gnosis would also have such an effect. Any of these would tend to increase the value of Mana and recovery thereof. Could be good.</li> <li>The free Reach only apply when casting a rote or praxis. Raises stakes on the books and deals for such things. That increases the chances of, say, strongarm tactics to get a grimoire made or a thief stealing a grimoire.</li> <li>Increase the costs of healing. Healing without life is far slower and with it is less mana-efficient. I'd add reach options to pop it back to normal if I was going that route.</li> <li>Reduce starting Arcana and increase Exp costs for Arcana &amp; Gnosis, possibly increasing the purchase costs and possibly increasing the costs more after 3.</li> <li>Any spell not narrated in a classical noir voice and description fails dramatically. A good Bogart impersonation should get a bonus die, at least.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T12:20:20-07:00","id":1105797,"title":"","content":"The last bullet point us great","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}